From dce4c4b1cd141591b7ecc969776a55f8c9920a9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:36:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 33/41] [TSReader] Take the segment PTS from the first audio
 frame, in 33 bits

The PTS diff of a segment came from the first PES with a PTS. When the
first audio PES of a segment has no PTS, the frames before that PES
moved the PTS diff of an audio stream by their duration, so the time
and a seek with that diff were off by those frames. At the start, the
frames before the first PTS took no diff. Now the first audio frame of
a segment sets the PTS of the stream in the segment, also when the
reader gives the frames before the first PTS the clock of that PTS. The
held frames then take the PTS diff of their segment. The video keeps
the PTS of the first video PES with a PTS: a video frame in a PES without a
PTS has the PTS of the PES before.

A PTS has 33 bits. The clock of the frames before a PTS and the clock
of the frames after the PTS in one PES now wrap after 0x1FFFFFFFF, as
the PTS of a PES of their own would.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
